{"task_id": "HumanEval/49", "solution": "def modp(n: int, p: int):\n    \"\"\"Return 2^n modulo p using modular exponentiation to handle large n efficiently.\n    This prevents overflow issues by applying the modulo operation at each step.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = 1\n    base = 2 % p  # The base for exponentiation, reduced modulo p\n\n    while n > 0:\n        if n % 2 == 1:  # If n is odd, multiply result by current base\n            result = (result * base) % p\n        base = (base * base) % p  # Square the base\n        n //= 2  # Halve the exponent n\n    return result"}
